---
description: Require regression tests for behavior changes and bug fixes
alwaysApply: true
---

# Regression tests are required

- Every bug fix must include a test that fails before the fix and passes after it.
- Every behavior change must add or update unit tests for the underlying logic.
- For interactive UI behavior, add a user-centric component test that exercises the relevant click, typing, keyboard, or submission flow.
- Assert observable behavior through accessible roles, labels, and visible outcomes; avoid implementation-detail assertions.
- Run the affected test suite and lint before considering the change complete.
- Do not delete or weaken a regression test merely to make a change pass; update it only when the intended behavior itself changed.
